[[:db/retract 17592186133272 :answer-field/choices 17592186133274] [:db/retract 17592186133272 :answer-field/choices 17592186133275] [:db/retract 17592186133272 :answer-field/choices 17592186133277] {:db/id 17592186133729 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-365bf094-f659-5822-bf63-2e5a6992d995"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186134539 :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X$ has the cumulative distribution function\n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & x<0 \\\\ 1-{e}^{-x}, & x\\ge 0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfind $P(X>2).$" :question/worked-solution "We can perform this computation using the complement, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>2) & =1-P(X\\le 2) \\\\  & =1-F(2) \\\\  & =1-(1-{e}^{-2}) \\\\  & ={e}^{-2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{e}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186133272 :answer-field/correct "answer-105177ed-381e-5551-8d54-f794cc7ae2f7" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f7ff0cb6-5ee6-5486-95b5-ba7fabd16b87" "answer-c6834059-6614-531c-86f9-081bd2ed69b6" "answer-105177ed-381e-5551-8d54-f794cc7ae2f7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f7ff0cb6-5ee6-5486-95b5-ba7fabd16b87" :answer/id #uuid "f7ff0cb6-5ee6-5486-95b5-ba7fabd16b87" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1-\\frac{1}{e}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c6834059-6614-531c-86f9-081bd2ed69b6" :answer/id #uuid "c6834059-6614-531c-86f9-081bd2ed69b6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1-\\frac{1}{{e}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-105177ed-381e-5551-8d54-f794cc7ae2f7" :answer/id #uuid "105177ed-381e-5551-8d54-f794cc7ae2f7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{e}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186133728 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-e65ef0d7-6649-5f56-9e79-7407f7595f66" "question-990f1bb6-e595-59df-8c02-d323344bc3ca"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-e65ef0d7-6649-5f56-9e79-7407f7595f66" :question/id #uuid "e65ef0d7-6649-5f56-9e79-7407f7595f66" :question/math-academy-id "q-89621" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{64}x(16-{x}^{2}),\\, & 0\\le x\\le 4 \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nits cumulative distribution function is \n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0,\\, & x<0 \\\\ h(x),\\, & 0\\le x\\le 4 \\\\ 1,\\, & x>4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the function $h(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Since our random variable $X$ has a probability density function $f(x)$ that is strictly positive only for $0<x<4,$ the cumulative distribution function takes the following form:\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & x<0 \\\\ {\\int }_{0}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t, & 0\\le x\\le 4 \\\\ 1, & x>4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the given probability density function, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{0}^{x}\\frac{1}{64}t(16-{t}^{2})\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\frac{1}{64}(8{t}^{2}-\\frac{{t}^{4}}{4})|}_{0}^{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{64}(8{x}^{2}-\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}-\\frac{{x}^{4}}{256}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the cumulative distribution function is given by\n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & x<0 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}-\\frac{{x}^{4}}{256}, & 0\\le x\\le 4 \\\\ 1, & x>4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-d0e871fb-e944-567c-b4fe-9835a0a9327f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-d0e871fb-e944-567c-b4fe-9835a0a9327f" :answer-field/id #uuid "d0e871fb-e944-567c-b4fe-9835a0a9327f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-5de59784-191d-59f0-ab4e-cb2aafa6fe90" :answer-field/choices ["answer-12f66496-4995-5d37-a001-943fa360d144" "answer-7295486c-b630-5ce0-8356-5ab47719adad" "answer-0c66a62f-9a33-540e-bb1b-485e50f03db9" "answer-af97dd8a-6b84-534d-9a5b-b7c3f09bac24" "answer-5de59784-191d-59f0-ab4e-cb2aafa6fe90"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-12f66496-4995-5d37-a001-943fa360d144" :answer/id #uuid "12f66496-4995-5d37-a001-943fa360d144" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{5{x}^{2}}{16}-\\frac{{x}^{4}}{64}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7295486c-b630-5ce0-8356-5ab47719adad" :answer/id #uuid "7295486c-b630-5ce0-8356-5ab47719adad" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}+\\frac{{x}^{4}}{256}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0c66a62f-9a33-540e-bb1b-485e50f03db9" :answer/id #uuid "0c66a62f-9a33-540e-bb1b-485e50f03db9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}-\\frac{{x}^{4}}{256}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-af97dd8a-6b84-534d-9a5b-b7c3f09bac24" :answer/id #uuid "af97dd8a-6b84-534d-9a5b-b7c3f09bac24" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}+\\frac{{x}^{4}}{256}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5de59784-191d-59f0-ab4e-cb2aafa6fe90" :answer/id #uuid "5de59784-191d-59f0-ab4e-cb2aafa6fe90" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}-\\frac{{x}^{4}}{256}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-365bf094-f659-5822-bf63-2e5a6992d995" :question/id #uuid "365bf094-f659-5822-bf63-2e5a6992d995" :question/math-academy-id "q-89745" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X$ has the cumulative distribution function\n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & x<1 \\\\ 1-\\frac{1}{{x}^{6}}, & x\\ge 1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfind $P(X\\le 2).$" :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a continuous random variable $X$ is the function $F(x)$ defined by\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nHence, the required probability is $F(2)=1-\\frac{1}{{2}^{6}}=\\frac{63}{64}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-20b56563-d267-5cfe-8c9b-169cce28e14c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-20b56563-d267-5cfe-8c9b-169cce28e14c" :answer-field/id #uuid "20b56563-d267-5cfe-8c9b-169cce28e14c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-cb9281eb-aea1-5259-9259-3205cf4277fd" :answer-field/choices ["answer-1a555ce7-328a-5393-a56d-7007de7c9835" "answer-921eed10-f9a7-592f-813f-d6d89b83f924" "answer-4760a79e-f036-5d0a-936b-74020feb11e9" "answer-cb9281eb-aea1-5259-9259-3205cf4277fd" "answer-2cdbdc75-2141-5c85-914f-cbf2e3062225"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1a555ce7-328a-5393-a56d-7007de7c9835" :answer/id #uuid "1a555ce7-328a-5393-a56d-7007de7c9835" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{63}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-921eed10-f9a7-592f-813f-d6d89b83f924" :answer/id #uuid "921eed10-f9a7-592f-813f-d6d89b83f924" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{64}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4760a79e-f036-5d0a-936b-74020feb11e9" :answer/id #uuid "4760a79e-f036-5d0a-936b-74020feb11e9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{61}{64}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cb9281eb-aea1-5259-9259-3205cf4277fd" :answer/id #uuid "cb9281eb-aea1-5259-9259-3205cf4277fd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{63}{64}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2cdbdc75-2141-5c85-914f-cbf2e3062225" :answer/id #uuid "2cdbdc75-2141-5c85-914f-cbf2e3062225" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{64}{63}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186133727 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-7e1280de-34a4-5310-b0ea-3ca5ec3ba975"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-7e1280de-34a4-5310-b0ea-3ca5ec3ba975" :question/id #uuid "7e1280de-34a4-5310-b0ea-3ca5ec3ba975" :question/math-academy-id "q-210763" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{5}{2}{e}^{-|5x|},\\,x\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\n$$\n\nits cumulative distribution function is\n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{e}^{5x}}{2},\\, & x<0 \\\\ h(x),\\, & x\\ge 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $h(x)=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Since our random variable $X$ has a probability distribution function $f(x)$ that involves an absolute value, the cumulative distribution function takes the following form:\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{x}\\frac{5}{2}{e}^{5t}\\,\\text{d}t, & x<0 \\\\ {\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}\\frac{5}{2}{e}^{5t}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{0}^{x}\\frac{5}{2}{e}^{-5t}\\,\\text{d}t, & x\\ge 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's compute the integrals.\n\n- If $x\\le 0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{x}\\frac{5}{2}{e}^{5t}\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\frac{{e}^{5t}}{2}|}_{-\\infty }^{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{5x}}{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}\\frac{5}{2}{e}^{5t}\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\frac{{e}^{5x}}{2}|}_{x=0} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- If $x>0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{x}\\frac{5}{2}{e}^{-5t}\\,\\text{d}t & =-{\\frac{{e}^{-5t}}{2}|}_{0}^{x} \\\\  & =-\\frac{{e}^{-5x}}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}\\frac{5}{2}{e}^{5t}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{0}^{x}\\frac{5}{2}{e}^{-5t}\\,\\text{d}t & =\\frac{1}{2}+(-\\frac{{e}^{-5x}}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =1-\\frac{{e}^{-5x}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the cumulative distribution function is given by\n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{e}^{5x}}{2}, & x<0 \\\\ 1-\\frac{{e}^{-5x}}{2}, & x\\ge 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-60abe397-ada8-52f7-89c3-1ccbe2f29023"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-60abe397-ada8-52f7-89c3-1ccbe2f29023" :answer-field/id #uuid "60abe397-ada8-52f7-89c3-1ccbe2f29023" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-65441b2f-7b3a-53c5-af33-45bf0ced0a21" :answer-field/choices ["answer-65441b2f-7b3a-53c5-af33-45bf0ced0a21"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-65441b2f-7b3a-53c5-af33-45bf0ced0a21" :answer/id #uuid "65441b2f-7b3a-53c5-af33-45bf0ced0a21" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1-\\frac{{e}^{-5x}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-990f1bb6-e595-59df-8c02-d323344bc3ca" :question/id #uuid "990f1bb6-e595-59df-8c02-d323344bc3ca" :question/math-academy-id "q-210785" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{2}{9}x+\\frac{8}{9},\\, & 1\\le x\\le 4 \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nits cumulative distribution function is \n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0,\\, & x<1 \\\\ h(x),\\, & 1\\le x\\le 4 \\\\ 1,\\, & x>4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $h(x)=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Since our random variable $X$ has a probability distribution function $f(x)$ that is strictly positive only for $1\\le x\\le 4,$ the cumulative distribution function takes the following form:\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & x<1 \\\\ {\\int }_{1}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t, & 1\\le x\\le 4 \\\\ 1, & x>4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the given probability density function, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{1}^{x}(-\\frac{2}{9}t+\\frac{8}{9})\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ \\text{ } & ={(-\\frac{1}{9}{t}^{2}+\\frac{8}{9}t)|}_{1}^{x} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{9}{x}^{2}+\\frac{8}{9}x-\\frac{7}{9} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{9}({x}^{2}-8x+7) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{9}(x-1)(x-7).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the cumulative distribution function is given by\n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & x<1 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{9}(x-1)(x-7), & 1\\le x\\le 4 \\\\ 1, & x>4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-45ff772f-b783-5f66-89ac-69df3d1d8f2a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-45ff772f-b783-5f66-89ac-69df3d1d8f2a" :answer-field/id #uuid "45ff772f-b783-5f66-89ac-69df3d1d8f2a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-da4529e7-604e-506b-adaa-ff85312c20f9" :answer-field/choices ["answer-da4529e7-604e-506b-adaa-ff85312c20f9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-da4529e7-604e-506b-adaa-ff85312c20f9" :answer/id #uuid "da4529e7-604e-506b-adaa-ff85312c20f9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{-x^{2}+8x-7}{9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-6e4f14fd-ece2-56c4-a9f7-319d868e1b1f" :activity/id #uuid "6e4f14fd-ece2-56c4-a9f7-319d868e1b1f" :activity/title "Cumulative Distribution Functions for Continuous Random Variables" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186050750 :activity/course 17592186046659 :activity/steps ["step-989b9a58-4363-5017-8054-1b3f417bd0d8" "step-443e51e5-e403-51ae-bbff-e563149f49e5" "step-24fe79a9-1c18-5367-b5d5-50f26230d23d" "step-cdf24c85-fec2-557e-990a-b96c38922ff0" "step-7a43148a-546c-5e25-817d-f6a542bfe3c4"] :activity/first-step "step-989b9a58-4363-5017-8054-1b3f417bd0d8" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-989b9a58-4363-5017-8054-1b3f417bd0d8" :step/id #uuid "989b9a58-4363-5017-8054-1b3f417bd0d8" :step/content 17592186134539 :step/next "step-443e51e5-e403-51ae-bbff-e563149f49e5" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-443e51e5-e403-51ae-bbff-e563149f49e5" :step/id #uuid "443e51e5-e403-51ae-bbff-e563149f49e5" :step/content "question-e65ef0d7-6649-5f56-9e79-7407f7595f66" :step/next "step-24fe79a9-1c18-5367-b5d5-50f26230d23d" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-24fe79a9-1c18-5367-b5d5-50f26230d23d" :step/id #uuid "24fe79a9-1c18-5367-b5d5-50f26230d23d" :step/content "question-365bf094-f659-5822-bf63-2e5a6992d995" :step/next "step-cdf24c85-fec2-557e-990a-b96c38922f